r zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 33.8% a year over five years.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 1.0% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 14, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","Analysts expect 16.1% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.5%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 4.0% a year to shareholders (4.0% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 0.8% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 30,000 employees, each generates about $1.3M of revenue, 2.6x the Consumer Defensive median, and productivity has risen 6.2% a year.","That works out to $32K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.8M (4x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":39,"head":"Avoid: priced 42% above its fair value of $74.91.","pros":["Revenue grew 11.5%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 7/9","Altman Z in the safe zone","12-1 month momentum +35%","Returns 4.0% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 42% above fair value of $74.91","ROIC 8.5% vs WACC 8.5%","Net debt/EBITDA 3.1x","P/E 29.8x vs sector 18.5x","EV/EBITDA 16.0x vs sector 10.3x"],"flags":["Priced 42% above its fair value of $74.91"],"need":[],"buy_below":63.67,"vc":{"base":74.91,"base_src":"dcf","bear":54.07,"bull":104.71,"alt_median":19.86,"n_alt":2,"gap":2.7709,"dispersion":0.655,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (65% dispersion)","DCF is 277% above the other models' median ($19.86)"]},"med":{"pe":18.5188,"ev_ebitda":10.2635,"pfcf":15.9681,"pb":2.0792,"roic":0.1185,"gross_margin":0.3401,"fcf_margin":0.0601,"div_yield":0.0296}},"ticker":"USFD","date":"2026-11-06"}